<title>ZIMBABWE: No change in Zimbabwe 1997 sugar output forecast.</title>
<headline>No change in Zimbabwe 1997 sugar output forecast.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zimbabwe's sugar production is still expected to hit a record 600,000 tonnes in 1997, in line with forecasts given earlier this year, a top industry official said on Friday.</p>
<p>David Rockliffe, general manager of Zimbabwe Sugar Sales, told reporters the expected increase in output was based on a good rainy season (November-April).</p>
<p>Zimbabwe produced 513,000 tonnes of sugar in 1996.</p>
<p>---Cris Chinaka, Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9.---</p>
